WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.083 --> 00:00:00.333
[camera flash]

00:00:01.418 --> 00:00:02.752
[applause]

00:00:02.752 --> 00:00:05.380
Dior:
People need to feel again.

00:00:05.380 --> 00:00:07.048
Dior:
They need to dream again.

00:00:07.048 --> 00:00:08.508
Dior:
They need to live again.

00:00:09.551 --> 00:00:12.345
Dior:
We can create a new world for them.

00:00:15.181 --> 00:00:18.393
This is a story about Christian Dior

00:00:18.393 --> 00:00:21.021
creating The New Look during World
War Two.

00:00:21.229 --> 00:00:24.190
Ben Mendelsohn:
He brought back fantasy and elegance

00:00:24.190 --> 00:00:26.443
Ben Mendelsohn:
in a difficult time for Paris.

00:00:27.360 --> 00:00:29.487
Todd A. Kessler:
The New Look was the name of Dior's

00:00:29.487 --> 00:00:32.532
iconic first collection in 1947.

00:00:33.450 --> 00:00:37.871
It symbolized healing
and brought a nation back on its feet.

00:00:38.455 --> 00:00:40.248
Juliette Binoche:
To understand fashion today,

00:00:40.790 --> 00:00:42.709
you've got to understand The New Look.

00:00:45.378 --> 00:00:47.881
It's a time of great talent.

00:00:47.881 --> 00:00:51.301
John Malkovich:
Dior, Chanel, Balmain, Balenciaga,

00:00:51.301 --> 00:00:53.803
John Malkovich:
Givenchy, Pierre Cardin. 

00:00:54.637 --> 00:00:57.807
Todd A. Kessler:
Dior was a young designer, but Coco Chanel

00:00:57.807 --> 00:01:01.686
Todd A. Kessler:
was the grande dame of fashion and was a worldwide celebrity.

00:01:02.145 --> 00:01:05.148
I explore the dark layers of her life.

00:01:05.732 --> 00:01:07.525
Juliette Binoche:
Humanity is complex.

00:01:07.525 --> 00:01:09.652
Life is not all black and white.

00:01:10.945 --> 00:01:12.655
Have you ever thought about

00:01:12.655 --> 00:01:15.617
Chanel:
what a woman has to face to survive in this world?

00:01:16.201 --> 00:01:18.953
You men and your wars, your rules.

00:01:19.996 --> 00:01:23.041
Todd A. Kessler:
These icons were forced to make challenging decisions

00:01:23.041 --> 00:01:24.417
Todd A. Kessler:
during World War Two.

00:01:24.417 --> 00:01:28.004
Ben Mendelsohn:
Dior's sister, Catherine, is a resistance fighter.

00:01:28.046 --> 00:01:31.674
Maisie Williams:
We feel we know so much about these figures.

00:01:32.008 --> 00:01:34.511
But this story really dared to explore 

00:01:34.511 --> 00:01:36.930
 the sides that we had not really considered before. 

00:01:39.641 --> 00:01:43.436
This is a story of survival and resilience.

00:01:43.436 --> 00:01:44.104
[laughs]

00:01:44.104 --> 00:01:49.150
Fashion needs a great collection to rise
from the ashes of the last five years.

00:01:50.068 --> 00:01:55.406
Creation is our survival, our salvation.

00:01:56.783 --> 00:01:58.201
We can interpret the pain

00:01:58.201 --> 00:02:01.538
Maisie Williams:
in the world through creativity.

00:02:01.621 --> 00:02:04.833
We have the capacity
as human beings to transform.

00:02:05.333 --> 00:02:08.503
And that spark is a beautiful spark.

00:02:10.505 --> 00:02:12.841
Catherine Dior:
It's time to show the world what you've created.

